<title>MEXICO: Clinton names banker Harmon to run ExIm Bank.</title>
<headline>Clinton names banker Harmon to run ExIm Bank.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House said on Tuesday that President Bill Clinton has nominated James Harmon, senior chairman of investment bank Schroder Wertheim &amp; Co. Inc., as chairman and president of the Export-Import Bank.</p>
<p>In a separate statement released in Mexico, where Clinton is on a state visit, it said he had also nominated Jackie Clegg as vice chairman and first vice president of the bank. Clegg is currently a vice president at the bank.</p>
<p>The Export-Import Bank facilitates export financing of U.S. goods and services by matching export credit subsidies from foreign governments and by absorbing credit risks that are beyond the scope of the private sector.</p>
</text>
